  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__intro": "Sreadya Privacy Policy. Account-free Sreadya and account-based Sreadya are equal first-class experiences. Core health tools remain available without an account, while optional end-to-end encrypted continuity adds cross-device convenience without creating a developer-readable reproductive-health database.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__lastUpdated": "Last updated",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section10__dot__body": "This policy, in-product privacy information and applicable store declarations must stay aligned with the features and services actually available in each release. External services and store availability are represented only when they are actually configured or published.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section10__dot__title": "Policy and release truth",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section1__dot__body": "You can use Sreadya without an account. Cycle tracking, logging, predictions, insights, reminders, reports, privacy controls and encrypted backup remain local-first core health features. Disabling sync does not disable local Sreadya.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section1__dot__title": "Account-free and local core",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section2__dot__body": "If you enable optional continuity, your health content is encrypted before leaving an authorized device. The synchronization service receives ciphertext, wrapped key or recovery material and only the minimum operational metadata needed for account/device authorization and synchronization. Sreadya infrastructure does not possess the health-vault decryption key.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section2__dot__title": "Account and encrypted continuity",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section3__dot__body": "Operational metadata can include opaque account, device, vault, object or event identifiers, ciphertext size, protocol/version counters, synchronization timestamps, public device-verification material, and authorization or revocation state. It does not authorize the service to receive readable period dates, symptoms, sexual activity, fertility observations, pregnancy state, medication details, private notes, prediction inputs or report contents.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section3__dot__title": "Minimum operational metadata",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section4__dot__body": "Account access and old-vault decryption are separate. Where a release enables verified email or SMS recovery, email or SMS can help recover account identity but cannot by itself decrypt the old health vault. A trusted device can approve a new device, while the independent recovery key can restore vault continuity. Losing every trusted device and the recovery key can make the previous vault unrecoverable.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section4__dot__title": "Account recovery and trusted devices",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section5__dot__body": "Local records remain until you edit or delete them, wipe Sreadya data, uninstall the client, or replace them with a validated restore. Account deletion removes server-side account and synchronized ciphertext state controlled by Sreadya. Sreadya cannot remotely erase former device copies, screenshots, user-created export files, CycleVault backups or data already sent to another destination; those copies must be deleted where they are stored.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section5__dot__title": "Retention and deletion",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section6__dot__body": "Reports, partner summaries, QR codes, CycleVault backups and other exports leave Sreadya only after explicit user action. CycleVault uses a user-held backup passphrase and remains separate from account-continuity recovery.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section6__dot__title": "Sharing, reports and backups",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section7__dot__body": "Health Connect and Apple Health are optional, permission-scoped integrations. Their platform stores remain separate systems under their providers’ rules, and permissions can be revoked through the operating system.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section7__dot__title": "Health integrations",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section8__dot__body": "Sreadya does not use advertising SDKs, behavioral analytics, remote session replay or developer health-payload telemetry. Diagnostics are limited to reviewed operational status and must not contain readable reproductive-health payloads.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section8__dot__title": "Diagnostics and analytics",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section9__dot__body": "Email or SMS verification providers are used only if those channels are enabled for a release. If enabled, they may process contact and delivery metadata under their own terms. App stores, operating systems, notification services, platform health stores and destinations chosen by the user are separate data flows.",
  "sreadya_privacyPolicy__dot__section9__dot__title": "Email, SMS and external providers",
  "sreadya_privacy__dot__boundaryBody": "Web PIN locking is available, but Sreadya does not call it native biometric security. The browser controls screenshots and app-switcher previews, and native HealthKit / Health Connect require the native clients.",
  "sreadya_privacy__dot__boundaryEyebrow": "Truthful boundary",
  "sreadya_privacy__dot__boundaryNote": "Account-free use remains first class. The encrypted local vault is authoritative, and Sreadya does not require reproductive-health telemetry to operate.",
  "sreadya_privacy__dot__boundaryTitle": "Platform protections are not exaggerated",
