  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open Cycle",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section1__dot__body": "Start or end a period, backdate or correct dates, and delete mistakes from the encrypted local record.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section1__dot__title": "Record and correct",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section2__dot__action": "Log reproductive context",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section2__dot__body": "Record spotting, light, medium or heavy flow and add optional private cycle notes or reproductive observations.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section2__dot__title": "Flow and context",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section3__dot__action": "Open Calendar",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section3__dot__body": "Use monthly, timeline and year views to review the history you entered. Historical editing remains available.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__cycle__dash__tracking__dot__section3__dot__title": "History that stays editable",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__intro": "A report exists only after you choose a date range and categories, preview the result, and explicitly export it.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section1__dot__action": "Build a report",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section1__dot__body": "Select dates and categories such as periods, flow, symptoms, pain, temperature/ovulation observations and optional notes.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section1__dot__title": "Choose the scope",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section2__dot__action": "Preview locally",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section2__dot__body": "Sensitive categories are not silently added. The preview is generated locally before CSV or PDF export becomes available.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section2__dot__title": "Preview before sharing",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section3__dot__action": "Review data controls",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section3__dot__body": "Sreadya does not upload the report to create it. Export is an explicit user action.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__doctor__dash__reports__dot__section3__dot__title": "You decide what leaves",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__intro": "Choose the Sreadya client that is actually available. This static site does not invent an App Store or Play Store listing that has not been published.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section1__dot__action": "Install the PWA",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section1__dot__body": "Open the full account-free Web client in a browser or install it to the Home Screen/Desktop for a focused standalone experience.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section1__dot__title": "Web / PWA · available now",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section2__dot__action": "Android guidance",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section2__dot__body": "The Android client follows the same Sreadya experience. Until a production store/download channel is published, use reviewed Android/PWA guidance rather than an unverified package link.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section2__dot__title": "Android",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section3__dot__action": "iPhone guidance",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section3__dot__body": "Native iOS distribution is shown only when available. The reviewed Safari Add to Home Screen path provides the current installable Web option.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__download__dot__section3__dot__title": "iPhone / iPad",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__intro": "Start with the task you need. Sreadya keeps recovery, privacy and health actions explicit rather than hiding them behind a generic support form.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open backup & restore",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section1__dot__body": "Use CycleVault to create a user-chosen encrypted backup and validate it before restore.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section1__dot__title": "I want to back up or restore",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section2__dot__action": "Open Privacy Center",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section2__dot__body": "The Privacy Center shows health-data location, local encryption, notification privacy, partner access, devices and diagnostics.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section2__dot__title": "I want to understand privacy",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section3__dot__action": "Open Diagnostics",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section3__dot__body": "Generate a sanitized diagnostics preview. It intentionally excludes period dates, symptoms, notes, sexual activity and fertility/pregnancy payloads.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__help__dot__section3__dot__title": "Something technical is wrong",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__intro": "Sreadya separates your local health experience from optional continuity. Tracking, predictions, insights and reports run on the client; account services never become the health-intelligence engine.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open private Sreadya",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section1__dot__body": "Period history, observations, preferences and local intelligence live in the encrypted Sreadya vault on this device.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section1__dot__title": "1 · Your device is authoritative",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section2__dot__action": "Read about predictions",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section2__dot__body": "Prediction v1, insights, reminder planning, reports and the deterministic assistant use local health history rather than sending reproductive-health plaintext to analytics or a cloud AI service.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section2__dot__title": "2 · Intelligence stays local",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section3__dot__action": "See the sync boundary",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section3__dot__body": "When an approved identity/sync service is configured, clients encrypt health content before synchronization. Account-free Sreadya remains complete without that service.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__how__dash__it__dash__works__dot__section3__dot__title": "3 · Continuity is optional",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__intro": "Insights summarize your records; they do not invent diagnoses. Sreadya explains the data range and sources behind an observation.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open Insights",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section1__dot__body": "Average, shortest and longest cycle, period duration and variation are calculated from your own valid history.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section1__dot__title": "Cycle statistics",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section2__dot__action": "Review patterns",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section2__dot__body": "Review flow, symptom, PMS, mood, pain and sleep patterns when enough local observations exist.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section2__dot__title": "Patterns you recorded",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section3__dot__action": "Review accuracy",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section3__dot__body": "When actual period outcomes exist, Sreadya can evaluate historical prediction accuracy without turning the result into a medical explanation.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__insights__dot__section3__dot__title": "Prediction accuracy",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__intro": "Sreadya adapts context across regular cycles, trying to conceive, pregnancy, postpartum, breastfeeding, perimenopause, menopause transition and hormonal contraception.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open Life Stage",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section1__dot__body": "Changing life-stage mode changes presentation and relevant estimates; it never erases health history you already recorded.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section1__dot__title": "Change context without deleting history",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section2__dot__action": "See prediction boundaries",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section2__dot__body": "Optional fertility-oriented estimates can be shown in this context while keeping the non-contraceptive and non-diagnostic boundary explicit.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section2__dot__title": "Trying to conceive",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section3__dot__action": "Read the privacy model",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section3__dot__body": "Life-stage settings are stored in the encrypted local Sreadya vault and do not require an account.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__life__dash__stages__dot__section3__dot__title": "Your mode is private",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__intro": "Predictions are estimates from your own valid cycle history. Sreadya shows uncertainty and confidence instead of pretending future biology is certain.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open Predictions",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section1__dot__body": "See the most likely next-period date, a wider expected window, confidence and cycle-length trend.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section1__dot__title": "Expected date and window",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section2__dot__action": "Review prediction history",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section2__dot__body": "The browser stores prediction history locally with the algorithm version and input reference so later outcomes can be evaluated.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section2__dot__title": "History and accuracy",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section3__dot__action": "Review life-stage context",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section3__dot__body": "Ovulation and fertile-window estimates appear only where enabled by life-stage context. They are not certified contraception or a clinical fertility guarantee.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__predictions__dot__section3__dot__title": "Fertility boundary",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__intro": "Privacy is an operating rule: account-free equality, encrypted local storage, no reproductive-health analytics payload and truthful platform limitations.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open Vault",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section1__dot__body": "Health records are encrypted before IndexedDB persistence. The browser-local vault remains authoritative.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section1__dot__title": "Encrypted local vault",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section2__dot__action": "Open privacy settings",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section2__dot__body": "Web supports a local PIN gate and automatic lock. Sreadya does not rename that into native biometric security, and the browser controls screenshots and app-switcher previews.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section2__dot__title": "PIN and platform boundaries",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section3__dot__action": "Open Privacy Center",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section3__dot__body": "The Privacy Center links backup/export, connected-device state, partner sharing, notification privacy, account boundaries and sanitized diagnostics.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__privacy__dot__section3__dot__title": "Review and revoke",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__intro": "The current Web release makes Sreadya easier to explore and use, with clearer workspaces, privacy controls and honest availability across devices.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section1__dot__action": "Explore features",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section1__dot__body": "The More hub and Features page make Sreadya tools easy to discover and open from a clear, consistent structure.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section1__dot__title": "Clear navigation",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section2__dot__action": "Open Sreadya",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section2__dot__body": "Logging, prediction history, personal reminders, privacy controls, diagnostics and account or continuity status are available from the Web workspace.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section2__dot__title": "Full Web workspace",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section3__dot__action": "Read security",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section3__dot__body": "Each release is checked for navigation, privacy, offline behavior and core user journeys before it is published.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__release__dash__notes__dot__section3__dot__title": "Privacy and reliability checks",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__intro": "A private 3-day-before-period reminder is the default. You can change cycle reminders, personal reminder families, time, quiet hours, snooze and notification privacy.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open Reminders",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section1__dot__body": "New local vaults enable the discreet 3-day cycle reminder by default. Seven-day, one-day, expected-day and late reminders remain adjustable.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section1__dot__title": "Private default",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section2__dot__action": "Manage personal reminders",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section2__dot__body": "Create medication, contraception-context, supplement, ovulation-test, pregnancy-test or custom wellness reminders and choose a snooze interval.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section2__dot__title": "Personal reminder families",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section3__dot__action": "Check Reminder Health",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section3__dot__body": "Reminder Health shows permission, time zone, installed-PWA state and the next intent. Closed-app delivery is only claimed when the browser and reviewed delivery path can provide it.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__reminders__dot__section3__dot__title": "Browser-adapted delivery",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dash__report__dot__intro": "This legacy route is retained for compatibility. The canonical security-reporting page is /security/report.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dash__report__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open security reporting",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dash__report__dot__section1__dot__body": "Security reporting guidance lives at the architecture-approved nested route.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dash__report__dot__section1__dot__title": "Use the canonical route",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__intro": "Sreadya fails closed around keys, health plaintext and release evidence. Security boundaries are separate for the local vault, optional continuity and software delivery.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__intro": "Report security issues with the minimum technical information needed to reproduce the problem. Do not attach real menstrual, fertility, pregnancy, sexual-activity or medication records.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section1__dot__action": "Generate sanitized diagnostics",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section1__dot__body": "Describe the affected route/version, browser or device, reproducible technical steps and observed security impact.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section1__dot__title": "What to include",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section2__dot__body": "Do not share vault keys, recovery secrets, passphrases or real health payloads in a security report.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section2__dot__title": "What not to include",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section3__dot__action": "Back to Security",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section3__dot__body": "Use synthetic values when a reproduction needs example data. Sreadya diagnostics are designed around allowlisted technical state.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__report__dot__section3__dot__title": "Preserve user privacy",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section1__dot__action": "Review backup controls",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section1__dot__body": "Health records use authenticated encryption. Backup restore validates integrity and compatibility before replacing live health data.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section1__dot__title": "Local cryptography",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section2__dot__action": "Read the continuity model",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section2__dot__body": "The sync protocol transports authenticated ciphertext and operational metadata; the service is not supposed to receive readable health content.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section2__dot__title": "Optional E2EE continuity",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section3__dot__action": "Security reporting",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section3__dot__body": "Security reports should contain technical reproduction information, not exported health records.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__security__dot__section3__dot__title": "Responsible reporting",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__boundary": "Encrypted continuity is available only when a compatible service is configured. Until then, Sreadya keeps continuity controls clearly unavailable rather than pretending to sync.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__intro": "Cross-device continuity is optional. Sreadya remains fully usable account-free when continuity is not configured.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section1__dot__action": "Open Sync status",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section1__dot__body": "Logging and local intelligence keep working when continuity is unavailable. Sreadya shows the real connection state rather than pretending a sync succeeded.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section1__dot__title": "Local-first during outage or absence",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section2__dot__action": "Review security",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section2__dot__body": "When continuity is configured, clients encrypt locally and the service stores opaque ciphertext plus minimum operational metadata.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section2__dot__title": "Ciphertext-only service boundary",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section3__dot__action": "Review device state",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section3__dot__body": "Device enrollment, revocation, passkey identity and recovery require optional continuity. When unavailable, those controls remain clearly disabled rather than simulated.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__sync__dot__section3__dot__title": "Trusted devices and recovery",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__intro": "Sreadya is a personal tracking and wellness product. Its estimates and observations are not a substitute for professional medical diagnosis, treatment or emergency care.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section1__dot__action": "Understand predictions",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section1__dot__body": "Expected dates, PMS, ovulation or fertile-window estimates can be uncertain and must not be treated as guarantees.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section1__dot__title": "Predictions are estimates",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section2__dot__action": "Review reproductive-health boundaries",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section2__dot__body": "The initial release does not claim contraceptive effectiveness or a certified avoid-pregnancy method.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section2__dot__title": "No certified contraception claim",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section3__dot__action": "Review privacy",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section3__dot__body": "Doctor reports, partner summaries and diagnostics require explicit user actions and have separate scopes.",
  "sreadya_publicTopic__dot__terms__dot__section3__dot__title": "You control exports and sharing",
  "sreadya_recovery__dot__body": "Sreadya can validate a user-held recovery key against a reviewed encrypted recovery package locally. The recovered vault-root secret is not displayed and is cleared immediately after verification.",
  "sreadya_recovery__dot__boundaryBody": "Email or SMS may help recover account identity when a reviewed provider is configured, but Email or SMS cannot unlock the old health vault and neither can independently decrypt it.",
  "sreadya_recovery__dot__boundaryEyebrow": "Boundary",
  "sreadya_recovery__dot__boundaryNote": "If every trusted device and the recovery key are lost, old encrypted vault continuity can become unrecoverable. That is part of the E2EE guarantee.",
  "sreadya_recovery__dot__boundaryTitle": "Email or SMS is not a vault key",
